WEBVTT

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:53.770
Do what's right, 
and everything will work out.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.110
Help, please!

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.020
I can't go on like this.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.470
Creatures of the Deep Sea

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.860
Shiba Inu Moving Services

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.950
<i>These are the first shoes 
I bought in Tokyo.</i>

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:54.460
<i>I bought them hoping 
I could be like them one day.</i>

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.580
<i>I never ended up using them.</i>

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.470
<i>So much for my dream.</i>

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.730
D&M Urban Association

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.730
Tsuji Music Promotion

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.730
Tsuji Music Promotion

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.730
Hashimoto Accounting

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:10.730
Kids these are so quick to quit.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:11.770
Seishun TEENS!

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:12.610
First Love Town

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.560
She was probably never
serious about it to begin with.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.360
She's naïve if she thinks she can get away 
with giving up her opportunity to someone else.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.500
True.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.420
She's been losing popularity lately.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.120
I guess she wasn't cut out for it.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.740
She's pretty, 
but she never really stood out.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:28.300
She might end up regretting it after she quits 
and learns how tough the real world is.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.090
I finished the paperwork 
for my school transfer.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.820
The moving truck left, too, 
so I'll be heading back home.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.380
Yeah?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.740
Good work, Fuuka.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:42.170
Thank you for all your help.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.810
Senpai!

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.880
Ruka-chan.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.740
I heard from the manager, 
so I wanted to see you.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.950
This was my fault, wasn't it?

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.990
It's because I stole your
opportunity, Fuuka-senpai.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.230
No, not at all.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.720
It was my decision to quit.

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.040
I'm sorry!

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.780
It's all right.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.740
Just do one thing for me.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.130
Senpai?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.130
Work hard. For my sake, too.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.250
Hello?

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.520
<i>Fuuka.</i>

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:30.810
<i>How's it going?</i>

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.430
I'm about to buy a ticket.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:35.480
<i>Sorry I couldn't go to help.</i>

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.780
<i>It happened at the same time 
as the neighborhood association trip.</i>

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.050
It's fine.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:41.020
I didn't have that much to carry, after all.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.530
I should be in Morioka by evening.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.090
Dad will be waiting for you at home.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.710
You don't have to worry about anything 
when you get home.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.330
I told the neighbors what's going on, too.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.120
<i>What?</i>

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.720
This kind of news spreads 
even if you try to hide them.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.560
Everyone's looking forward

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.140
<i>to seeing you back home.</i>

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.690
Who's "everyone"?

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:02.960
<i>Granny Sasaki, Akko-neechan, and others.</i>

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:07.160
<i>They're all set on throwing a party 
to cheer you up.</i>

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.700
<i>Entertainment isn't exactly 
stable work, anyway.</i>

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:14.010
<i>Everyone says you made
the right move, quitting early.</i>

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:18.620
<i>I should get going.</i>

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:19.800
<i>Get home safe.</i>

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.700
<i>Contact me when you get home.</i>

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.450
A party to cheer me up?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.950
<b>Cheer Up Fuuka-chan Party</b>

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.230
No way.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.710
<b>I know! Okinawa!</b>

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.960
<b>Okinawa</b>

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.470
<b>Welcome to Okinawa</b>

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.470
I actually came.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.300
We're finally here!

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.880
Where should we go first?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.480
The beach, obviously.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.310
I can see it.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.360
There's something weighing on you.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:37.020
I can see everything.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.760
Um...

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.600
Are you a fortune teller?

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.580
Your right hand.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:48.180
Oh, dear!

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.790
Do you want to know?

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.780
Y-Yeah!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.160
3,000 yen for ten minutes.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:04.720
You're the insular, studious type 
without much street smarts.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.050
You don't know how to say "no."

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.790
From the condition of your skin, 
you're in your late teens.

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:11.260
You're right!

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.470
You traveled on your own from Tokyo.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.410
Wow, that's so specific!

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:19.210
I can just tell.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.270
U-Um...

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:24.950
What is such a talented fortune teller 
like you doing in such a small shop?

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:31.480
And then my husband cheated on me, too.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:33.980
I've got such horrible luck.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:36.090
That's disappointing.

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:37.290
Oh, yeah.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:41.380
I want you to have this 
to help you feel better.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.140
You're a good girl.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.580
Oh, the time...

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:47.670
All right.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.150
I'll give you my best reading.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.890
Write down your birthday here.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.040
You haven't had much good fortune lately.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:02.700
You're lost right now.

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:08.090
Head toward Sagittarius. 
It shows up around sunset.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.650
You'll have a good encounter there.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:17.190
O-Okay.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.450
No, no.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:27.130
There's a phrase in Okinawa: 
"Meet once, and we're siblings."

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.600
There must have been a reason 
that we met each other.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.850
We'll help each other out 
in times of need.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.140
Thank you.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.640
Sagittarius...

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:34.950
<i>It feels so nice here.</i>

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.110
<i>I'll figure it out.</i>

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.490
<b>The Tropical Fish Ran Away</b>

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:42.060
Hair, check!

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:43.800
Nails, check!

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:46.060
Smell is... all right!

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:52.230
Morning!

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.230
Wow, this looks delicious!

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.560
Kai-kun gave it to us.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.240
Thank you.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:03.460
So good!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:07.460
Grams, I have a late shift today.

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:09.770
I'm going straight after class.

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.160
All right.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:13.680
I'm meeting someone in Naha later.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:15.310
About the shipment?

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:16.260
That's right.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Notifications</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Call</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>6 hours ago</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Mom</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>3 calls</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Message</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>7 hours ago</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Mom</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Contact me</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Call</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>7 hours ago</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Mom</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.600
<b>Missed call</b>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:31.100
<b>Will you be home soon?</b>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:31.100
<b>I heard you aren't home yet. 
What's going on?</b>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:31.100
<b>I'm not at home, 
but contact me whenever you can.</b>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:31.100
<b>I want to hear what's going on. 
Please contact me.</b>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:31.100
<b>Sorry, Mom. I forgot I'd promised 
to stay over at my friend's place.</b>

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.100
<b>I'll contact you when I'm coming home.</b>

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.110
<b>Slide to turn off</b>

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.510
Bye!

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.280
Morning, Kai, Udon-chan.

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.080
I thought you'd be here.

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.220
Do you have remedial classes, too, Kukuru?

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.520
I missed too much school.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:05.120
You're working too hard.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:07.120
Well, I have so much to do.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.140
Oh, yeah. 
The banana fish was delicious.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:10.910
I caught it.

00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:12.270
Take me there again next time.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.160
Okay, sure.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.020
Is that a date?

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:15.740
Fishing.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:17.260
So it's just work.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.770
You know, Kukuru...

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:25.740
I wish you'd have more interest 
not just in fish but in humanity.

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:28.250
And in class.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:32.760
Misakino, what is this math report 
you submitted?

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:34.290
<b>Squid-Raising Journal</b>

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:34.290
A squid-raising journal.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:35.450
Why?

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.080
Why squid for math?

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:40.940
The world of squid is more 
interesting than math.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:43.680
I mean, it was well-written, but...

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:45.600
You know, Sensei...

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.080
Squid live for only about a year.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.780
And sometimes they jump out of the tank 
and turn into dried squid.

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:53.150
They're really hard to raise.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.880
But the more you watch them, 
the more adorable they are.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.770
Sensei, can you start class please?

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.580
This isn't getting anywhere.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:00.250
I know.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.400
Ouch!

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.750
<b>Parenting Journal</b>

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.750
<b>Misakino Kukuru</b>

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:21.740
So hot...

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:26.760
Where did my hat go?

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.700
Are you all right?

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:48.480
First off, here.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.270
You should stay hydrated.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:51.980
To avoid heat stroke.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:56.350
And try to cool your lymph nodes, 
under your neck, and under your armpits.

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.910
Okay.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:03.020
I feel so much better.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.400
Are you here on vacation?

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.050
Yes.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.680
<b>Oujima</b>

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:16.170
<i>An attractive girl, traveling alone.</i>

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:17.360
<i>No car.</i>

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:18.940
<i>Kind of quiet.</i>

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.810
<i>Is something wrong with her?</i>

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.910
If you're looking for a place nearby...

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:29.160
How about these?

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:37.420
<b>Sefa-utaki</b>

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.540
<b>Azama Sansan Beach</b>

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.540
<b>Nanjo-shi City, Okinawa</b>

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.420
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium</b>

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.380
Here's my card.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.210
I'll give you a ride, if you like.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.180
<b>Heart City Nanjo</b>

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.180
<b>Nanjo-shi City Tourism Association</b>

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:26.210
<b>Welcome to Gama Gama Aquarium</b>

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:25.220
That's so cute.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.720
<b>One-Day Ticket</b>

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.720
<b>One Adult</b>

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.720
<b>500 yen</b>

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.720
<b>Entry Tickets</b>

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.250
<b><i>Naso vlamingii</i></b>

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.250
<b><i>Epinephelus merra</i> Bloch</b>

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.250
<b><i>Diodon holacanthus</i></b>

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.250
<b><i>Gymnothorax isingteena</i></b>

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.250
<b><i>Heniochus acuminatus</i></b>

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
<b>1 hama</b>

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
<b>2 kuma</b>

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
<b>3 kakure</b>

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
<b>is the way 
to remember!</b>

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
<b>Clownfish look alike, 
but they're each a bit different!</b>

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
<b>Hamakumanomi (brindled anemone-fish) 
One white stripe</b>

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
<b>Kumanomi (<i>Amphiprion clarkii</i>) 
Two white stripes</b>

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
<b>Kakurekumanomi (<i>Amphiprion ocellaris</i>) 
Three white stripes</b>

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.060
Hello!

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.240
Kuuya-san.

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:26.400
'Sup.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:27.880
You have work today?

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:31.200
Umi-yan's still off work 
with a bad back.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.420
Gramps seems busy.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:35.340
He got handed more work.

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:36.700
Seriously?

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.790
We'd have been screwed 
if you weren't on summer break.

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:43.040
<b>Tank Number 6</b>

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.400
How's the hand-off?

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:43.040
I recorded it in the journal.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.590
How's the traffic?

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.060
Same as usual.

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:50.050
Maybe the human race has ended 
or something.

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.060
I'm going to go look around.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.150
So pretty.

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:13.940
No one's going to notice 
you hiding in that corner, you know.

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:17.200
You're like me, huh?

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:23.900
Ecsenius yaeyamaensis?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:27.460
"Not the most noticeable fish, 
but the hardest-working."

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:33.970
"It eats the moss off rocks and glass, 
keeping the tank clean for us."

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.880
I was hard-working, too.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:42.950
But I guess it isn't enough 
to be hard-working.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>New song:</b>

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>Love Clover</b>

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>Center:</b>

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>Miyazawa Fuuka</b>

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>Subs:</b>

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>Shiroi Ruka</b>

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>Miyamori Aoi</b>

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.580
<i>I worked so hard.</i>

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:54.980
Thanks.

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:56.820
But...

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:00.380
it's over.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:01.420
It's all over.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:04.480
My dreams, my aspirations...

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:09.000
I don't have anything.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:55.960
Did you just see <i>it</i>?

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:56.840
Huh?

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.720
Aquariums are strange places, aren't they?

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:04.010
Strange creatures, strange ecologies...

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.890
You get a glimpse into something 
you don't normally get to see.

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:11.830
But sometimes, you see
something even more strange.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.150
What did I just see?

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:18.760
Don't tell anyone else, okay?

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.080
O-Okay.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:22.510
It was probably a kijimunaa 
playing tricks on you.

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:25.360
This place is old, so you
can expect things to happen.

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:26.970
At least, that's what Gramps said.

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:28.660
"Kijimunaa"?

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.490
Is this your first time here?

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:31.700
Y-Yes.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:34.090
I'll show you around.

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:34.830
But...

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:38.170
Welcome to Gama Gama Aquarium.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:41.220
I'm the director, Misakino Kukuru.

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:14.770
A gama is a kind of natural cave 
that shows up in a part of Okinawa.

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:20.030
A lot of sad things happened there 
during the war, but a long time ago,

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:23.270
they said it was a place that connected 
the real world to the underworld.

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:26.520
It's called the Gama Gama Aquarium

00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:29.000
because it's a strange place 
that's still near home.

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:30.280
Huh.

00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:35.040
It seems more laid-back than strange, though.

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:39.800
It's sorta like someone's
grandma's living room, too.

00:22:39.800 --> 00:22:41.040
I can see that.

00:22:42.310 --> 00:22:43.540
It's kind of nice, right?

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:52.920
So cute.

00:22:52.920 --> 00:22:54.140
Kukuru!

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:57.040
Come on. Is the pool ready yet?

00:22:57.040 --> 00:22:59.160
Sorry, next time.

00:22:59.160 --> 00:23:01.130
What? Why?

00:23:01.130 --> 00:23:02.880
Kukuru sucks!

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:03.900
Pool?

00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:07.020
The touch pool, 
where you can touch the animals.

00:23:07.020 --> 00:23:08.900
It's closed for a while.

00:23:09.890 --> 00:23:11.630
We don't have enough people.

00:23:11.630 --> 00:23:14.630
We've been trying to hire for a while, 
but no one's taken the job.

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:25.370
Hey!

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:27.050
Please.

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:29.300
Let me stay here!

00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:30.940
Huh?
